 coronary atherosclerosis</article-title><source>J Am Coll Cardiol</source><year>1997</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>57</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9207621</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Knez</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prediction of serious cardiovascular events by determining coronary artery calcification measured by multi-slice computed tomography</article-title><source>Dtsch Med Wochenschr</source><year>2005</year><volume>130</volume><fpage>2433</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16240241</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berman</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>ND</given-names></name><name><surname>Gransar</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Relationship between stress-induced myocardial ischemia and atherosclerosis measured by coronary calcium tomography</article-title><source>J Am Coll Cardiol</source><year>2004</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>923</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15312881</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bild</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Detrano</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Peterson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Ethnic differences in coronary calcification: the Multi-Ethnic Study of Atherosclerosis (MESA)</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>2005</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>1313</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15769774</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brindis</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Douglas</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hendel</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>ACCF/ASNC appropriateness criteria for single-photon emission computed tomography myocardial perfusion imaging (SPECT MPI): a report of the American College of Cardiology Foundation Quality Strategic Directions Committee Appropriateness Criteria Working Group and the American Society of Nuclear Cardiology endorsed by the American Heart Association</article-title><source>J Am Coll Cardiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>1587</fpage><lpage>605</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16226194</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Budoff</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Achenbach</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Blumenthal</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Assessment of coronary artery disease by cardiac computed tomography. A Statement from the American Heart Association Committee on Cardiovascular Imaging and Intervention, Council on Cardiovascular Radiology and Intervention, and Committee on Cardiac Imaging, Council on Clinical Cardiology</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>2006</year><volume>114</volume><fpage>1761</fpage><lpage>91</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17015792</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Budoff</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Raggi</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Berman</surname><given-names>D</given-n